  "reason": "The current best (config_043: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, acc=0.725) has exhausted all scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l multimodal multiprofile combinations. The remaining major uncertainty is whether the RNA encoder choice (scvi_n200 vs. alternatives) is the dominant factor or whether the architecture (transformer + weighted + ViT-L) is what drives performance. config_046 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) isolates the RNA encoder variable by swapping scvi_n200 for pca_n2000 while keeping the exact best architecture. While scgpt underperformed scvi_n200 by ~0.2, PCA at 2000 dimensions is a fundamentally different (linear, high-dimensional) representation that could capture complementary variance. As the final experiment, this is the highest-information test: if PCA approaches 0.725, it reveals the architecture is the key driver; if it falls well short, it confirms scvi_n200 is essential and solidifies config_043 as the definitive best. No other untested config has a plausible path to exceeding 0.725."
}

